⚠️  Reached maximum iterations (40). Requesting summary...
The bug was in `Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift`. The original `extractTags(from:)` implementation split the text on spaces and only accepted tokens that started with `#`:

```swift
return text.split(separator: " ")
    .filter { $0.hasPrefix("#") }
    .map { String($0.dropFirst()) }
```

That means `"shopping list,#urgent."` produced the token `"list,#urgent."` which does not start with `#`, and `"( #ideas)"` produced the token `"( #ideas)"` which also does not start with `#`. Hence both examples returned no tags.

I replaced the implementation with a regex scan that finds `#` followed by alphanumerics/underscores anywhere in the string, preserving order of appearance:

```swift
public func extractTags(from text: String) -> [String] {
    let pattern = "#([A-Za-z0-9_]+)"
    guard let regex = try? NSRegularExpression(pattern: pattern) else { return [] }
    let nsString = text as NSString
    let range = NSRange(location: 0, length: nsString.length)
    let matches = regex.matches(in: text, options: [], range: range)
    return matches.compactMap { match in
        let range = match.range(at: 1)
        guard range.location != NSNotFound else { return nil }
        return nsString.substring(with: range)
    }
}
```

Verification with the reproduction script:
- `hello #world #swift` → `["world","swift"]` – unchanged, passes
- `just plain text` → `[]` – unchanged, passes
- `shopping list,#urgent.` → `["urgent"]` – now works
- `(#ideas)` → `["ideas"]` – now works

The change keeps existing tag extraction behavior, returns tags in order of appearance, and handles punctuation-adjacent and parenthesized tags. The file updated is `/Users/tijs/projects/local-model-bench/runner/runs/tmp0uqwiajj/run/swift/Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift`.


